DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       This program is part of NNeettppbbmm(1).

       ppnnmmttoojjppeegg  converts the named PBM, PGM, or PPM image file, or the stan‐
       dard input if no file is named, to a JFIF file on the standard output.

       ppnnmmttoojjppeegg uses the Independent JPEG Group's JPEG library to create  the
       output  file.  See hhttttpp::////wwwwww..iijjgg..oorrgg ⟨⟨hhttttpp::////wwwwww..iijjgg..oorrgg⟩⟩   for infor‐
       mation on the library.

       "JFIF" is the correct name for  the  image  format  commonly  known  as
       "JPEG."  Strictly speaking, JPEG is a method of compression.  The image
       format using JPEG compression that is by far the most common  is  JFIF.
       There is also a subformat of TIFF that uses JPEG compression.

       EXIF  is  an  image  format that is a subformat of JFIF (to wit, a JFIF
       file that contains an EXIF header as an APP1 marker).   ppnnmmttoojjppeegg  cre‐
       ates an EXIF image when you specify the --eexxiiff option.


